}` to your `err` here too."],["c35b2b2e_b4272ec3",19,-2,1,"Can you add to this comment explaining why we don’t need to do anything here for the right bundle ID?"],["dc1e3ea8_a8b51352",19,-2,0,"Is the bundle ID the only signal (that we can discern) that Installer.app uses to decide to do its weird thing? I guess the test I have in mind for this is to create ONLY Google…"],["0cd5fcbb_2253a88b",19,0,1,"Small thing, but I’d use ``` \"hint: expected \\\"${BUNDLE_ID}\\\", found \\\"${existing_bundle_id}\\\"\" ``` The double-quoted strings read better in a wider variety of contexts than the single-quoted ones."],["599fffce_bc755475",19,0,1,"And since you do this pair together always, I’d refactor it into a common function, like `note_standard_hint` (and just put the strings in-line in that function)."],["d73e75cf_068208ec",19,0,1,"`elif` not needed after `exit`. This can just be `if`."],["dcb0c381_baa8f2bf",19,0,1,"Rather than trying to introspect into magic prefixes, I’d just change this function to accept two parameters. The first one could be `\"notice\"` or `\"error\"`."]],0,4818],[7551491,20493,134,3.848,3.085,[[38,1.0,159,126]],[["78cf2cd0_9f52473e",20,0,1,"→ that"],["8ffcbf93_8963e138",21,0,1,"This test should be renamed. It’s now about removing the quarantine attribute from a file that never had one set to begin with. That fact is more important than the fact that it does remove-remove. I…"],["e871c57c_c99e1aa6",20,0,1,"It always returns a boolean, not just if successful. (I get what you’re driving at with the comment edit, but strictly speaking, what was here before was more accurate in this regard.)"]],0,4819],[7532545,20496,84,2.538,2.075,[[250,0.393,4,34],[243,0.348,53,30],[251,0.157,3,13],[199,0.101,15,7]],[["077d986c_717e6f06",22,-2,1,"Not 0 in this case, but no longer necessary."],["7bebeb40_88e76402",22,-2,1,"and here."],["a486dffa_03b29353",22,-2,1,"Same here."],["a7746e15_bae196e8",22,-2,1,"VpnType.kIKEv2 is 0 so this will be false."],["baa29530_20b39fb8"